# The root spec of the to-do render: the target (Execution Contract Conformance 10).
# It carries what TARGET.md carried: the output stack, the UX and the existing systems.
# Sources: assets/design/todo-app.md "The rendered app" (Scott, 2026-11-25 11:07 AM Central), each line's ruling beside it.

Spec: Shared to-do list

# Hono on Bun (Scott, 2026-11-16); XTDB the default store, one store (2026-10-12, 2026-10-14).
# SpecDD 1.6 inherits Platform in child specs natively, so the platform line needs no extension of ours.
Platform: Hono on Bun, XTDB

Purpose:
  The render of the shared to-do list: an author hands a set of to-dos to a team in priority order, and the team claims them and checks them off.
  The intent is the app page and its pinned atoms in `.grace/`; this spec carries the render's target and no rule of the app.

Structure:
  ./.grace/
  ./CORNERS.md

References:
  ./.grace/todo.idd
  ./.grace/pins.tsv
  ./.grace/bootstrap.md
  ./CORNERS.md

Must:
  # Output stack.
  The code is lowered from the grammar tree through Hydra.
  # Scott, 2026-11-20; the 1.0 path of 2026-11-25.
  The app is hosted on Fly.
  # Scott, 2026-10-20; Unikraft after 1.0 (2026-11-23).
  # UX.
  The user interface is built on shadcn/ui, with INKs.
  # Scott, 2026-11-25 9:25 AM Central; INKs in every render (2026-11-10).
  The client is thin and a PWA, pulling only what it needs from a generated API that carries the store's validations.
  # Scott, 2026-11-19.
  The real app records usage events and runs A/B tests.
  # Scott, 2026-11-19.
  # Existing systems: none; the to-do app is new.

Must not:
  Hand-edit generated code or a contract: change the pattern and rebuild.
  # Scott, 2026-11-16: "We don't hack code ever".
